---
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#- THE ARCADE'S OWN ADDRESS (ARCADE-SPEC.md). Found through a door, the
   arcade opens over the page it was found on and this file is never
   loaded; this is for the shared link and a reload. One file for every
   language: the visitor's is the site's cookie, as on the 404. -#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>Thauma Arcade</title>
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#07090E">
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="/fonts/Sora-latin-v2.woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="/fonts/Inter-latin-v2.woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="icon" href="/img/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/main.css?v={{ "/css/main.css" | v }}">
<style>html,body{height:100%;background:#07090E;overflow:hidden}</style>
<script>
  (function () {
    var m = document.cookie.match(/thauma_lang=([a-z]{2})/);
    var langs = {{ activeLangs | dump | safe }};
    if (m && langs.indexOf(m[1]) !== -1) document.documentElement.lang = m[1];
  })();
</script>
</head>
<body class="arcade-page">
{#- Straight in: there is no page to break, so doors.js sees body.arcade-page
   and powers the arcade on by itself; Back leads to the site's home. -#}
{% include "arcade-doors.njk" %}
</body>
</html>
